  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Make the exponential bases agree",
      "body": "<p>Rewrite the power with base four using base two. Use equality of powers with the same positive base to compare their exponents.</p>",
      "recap": "Equal powers of a common positive base other than one have equal exponents.",
      "pitfall": "A power of a power multiplies the exponents.",
      "pause": "Obtain the trigonometric equation and record where tangent is defined.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l05",
          "reminder": "Equal powers of a common positive base other than one have equal exponents."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Preserve possible zero solutions",
      "body": "<p>Replace tangent by sine divided by cosine on its domain. Clear the permitted denominator, then factor the resulting equation.</p>",
      "recap": "Factoring retains the zero branch that division by a trig factor can discard.",
      "pitfall": "Multiplication does not restore inputs at which the original tangent was undefined.",
      "pause": "Solve every factor separately, keep the stated endpoints, check exclusions and count distinct inputs.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l04",
          "reminder": "Factoring retains the zero branch that division by a trig factor can discard."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><strong>1. State the domain and equate exponents.</strong> Tangent is undefined at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. On the remaining domain, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, so the equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>2. Factor without losing a zero branch.</strong> Multiply by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02260;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> to get <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>3. List the solutions.</strong> The sine-zero branch gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi></mrow></math>. The other branch has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, giving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#x003C0;</mi><mo>&#x0002F;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>. All are in the tangent domain and the sets are disjoint. There are 7 solutions. <strong>Answer F.</strong></p>",
